  "body": "The obligations define a fold over an unordered, duplicating delivery stream whose final state depends only on booking identity, revision, and time. The mechanism is: (1) deduplicate deliveries structurally, because identical immutable records carry no new information; (2) group by booking; (3) within each booking choose the greatest revision, breaking no ties because a booking/revision pair never conflicts; (4) classify only that latest revision: a release contributes 0, a hold contributes quantity only if expires_at > now, otherwise 0; (5) sum those contributions per item; (6) emit every stock row sorted by item, with available = capacity - reserved, allowing negative availability. Replay and reordering are harmless because the result is a function of the set of (booking, revision) records, not their delivery order; duplicate delivery is absorbed by structural deduplication. Expiry is a predicate on the latest revision's expires_at against input.now, so an expired hold vanishes entirely and cannot resurrect an older hold. Later cancellation works because a release is a strictly higher integer revision for the same booking, so it replaces all lower holds and contributes zero. Oversubscription is never clamped or filtered: reserved can exceed capacity and available becomes negative, which is the observable signal. The procedure assumes revision numbers are comparable integers, each booking has exactly one item, events name listed stock items, and no booking/revision pair carries contradictory content; an event for an unlisted item would make the account incomplete rather than falsify it, since the task guarantees events name listed items. A discriminating failure case is: booking b has revision 1 hold quantity 5 expires_at 20 and revision 2 hold quantity 2 expires_at 5, with now=10 and capacity 10. A delivery-order or incremental-delta implementation might count 5 or 5+2; the correct account discards revision 1, sees the latest hold expired, reserves 0, and reports available 10. Any revision of this program must preserve that the latest revision by integer order is authoritative and that duplicate delivery of the same record contributes once. The program is a direct expression of these steps using group-like selection via max_by, so it is not a lookup of the public examples.",
